IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sssa-nouns`

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 2: THE SCHEME.
--
-- s 5(1) is carried as the name and purpose of the Scheme.  ss 5(2) to 5(8)
-- (who administers it, deeming the Board's staff public officers, appointing
-- administrators and investigators, Gazette notices) are machinery; their effect
-- on the definitions in s 2 enters as facts.  s 6 is the only place the Act says
-- who is an eligible individual, and it leaves criterion (c) to regulations that
-- are not among the sources; s 7 leaves benefits, manner and amounts to the
-- same regulations.  Each such criterion, amount or manner is an INPUT.
--
-- Dates are `Date day month year`.  The age rules are calendar-component rules
-- built from the components, never by `add years`, which would clamp 29 February
-- to 28 February where s 6(2)(b) deems 1 March.

§ `Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 -- Part 2 -- Silver Support Scheme`

§§ `s 5 Establishment of the Scheme`

-- src:183 | 5.—(1) There is established a social security scheme, known as the
-- src:184 | Silver Support Scheme, for the purpose of providing financial support
-- src:185 | to eligible individuals.
@ref SSSA2015 s 5(1) (src:183-185)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 5(1) the name by which the established scheme is known` MEANS "Silver Support Scheme"

-- src:183 | 5.—(1) There is established a social security scheme, known as the
-- src:184 | Silver Support Scheme, for the purpose of providing financial support
-- src:185 | to eligible individuals.
@ref SSSA2015 s 5(1) (src:183-185)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 5(1) the purpose for which the Scheme is established` MEANS "providing financial support to eligible individuals"

§§ `s 6 Who is an eligible individual?`

-- s 6(2)(d): "where the month in which an individual was born cannot be
-- ascertained, that individual is deemed to be born in January".
-- s 6(2)(c): "where the day of the month ... cannot be ascertained, that
-- individual is deemed to be born on the first day of that month".
-- FORK F-2: where the month cannot be ascertained but the day can, the text deems
-- only the month, so the ascertained day is kept (15th of January, not 1st).
-- src:274 | (c) where the day of the month in which an individual was
-- src:275 | born cannot be ascertained, that individual is deemed to be
-- src:276 | born on the first day of that month; and
-- src:278 | (d) where the month in which an individual was born cannot
-- src:279 | be ascertained, that individual is deemed to be born in
-- src:280 | January.
@ref SSSA2015 s 6(2)(c) and (d) (src:274-280)
GIVEN birth IS A `Birth facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 6(2)(d) the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` MEANS
    fromMaybe 1 (birth's `month of birth`)

-- src:274 | (c) where the day of the month in which an individual was
-- src:275 | born cannot be ascertained, that individual is deemed to be
-- src:276 | born on the first day of that month; and
@ref SSSA2015 s 6(2)(c) (src:274-276)
GIVEN birth IS A `Birth facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 6(2)(c) the day of the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` MEANS
    fromMaybe 1 (birth's `day of birth`)

-- s 6(2)(a): the 65th anniversary of the date of birth.
-- s 6(2)(b): "where an individual was born on 29 February, the 65th anniversary
-- of the date of that individual's birth is deemed to occur on 1 March".
-- The anniversary is built from its components.  A birth on 29 February is in a
-- leap year, and 65 years later is never a leap year, so the day does not exist
-- and the Act's 1 March is the answer in every case.
-- src:267 | (a) an individual attains 65 years of age on the
-- src:268 | 65th anniversary of the date of that individual’s birth;
-- src:270 | (b) where an individual was born on 29 February, the
-- src:271 | 65th anniversary of the date of that individual’s birth is
-- src:272 | deemed to occur on 1 March;
@ref SSSA2015 s 6(2)(a) and (b) (src:267-272)
GIVEN `the year of birth` IS A NUMBER
      `the month of birth` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the month of birth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the month of birth` EQUALS 2 AND `the day of the month of birth` EQUALS 29
        THEN Date 1 3 (`the year of birth` PLUS 65)
        OTHERWISE Date `the day of the month of birth` `the month of birth` (`the year of birth` PLUS 65)

-- The date on which the individual attains 65.  A year of birth that cannot be
-- ascertained is not covered by s 6(2): the text deems a month and a day and
-- says nothing about the year.
-- src:265 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b) —
-- src:267 | (a) an individual attains 65 years of age on the
-- src:268 | 65th anniversary of the date of that individual’s birth;
@ref SSSA2015 s 6(2) (src:265-268)
GIVEN birth IS A `Birth facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` MEANS
    CONSIDER birth's `year of birth`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text deems the month and the day when they cannot be ascertained, and says nothing about the year
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST y THEN
        JUST (`s 6(2)(a) and (b) the 65th anniversary of the date of birth` y (`s 6(2)(d) the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` birth) (`s 6(2)(c) the day of the month of birth taken for s 6(1)(b)` birth))

-- s 6(1)(b): "has attained 65 years of age", asked as at a date the caller gives
-- (the text does not say as at when; the caller names the day of the question).
-- src:261 | (b) has attained 65 years of age; and
-- src:265 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b) —
-- src:267 | (a) an individual attains 65 years of age on the
-- src:268 | 65th anniversary of the date of that individual’s birth;
@ref SSSA2015 s 6(1)(b) (src:261-268)
GIVEN birth IS A `Birth facts`
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` birth
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no date of attaining 65 can be worked out without the year of birth
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST attains THEN
        IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST attains
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an individual attains 65 years of age on the 65th anniversary of the date of that individual’s birth"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 6(1): "an eligible individual is an individual who (a) is a citizen of
-- Singapore; (b) has attained 65 years of age; and (c) satisfies all other
-- eligibility criteria that may be prescribed".  The three limbs are read as a
-- definition, so any limb that fails answers JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a) in
-- NOTES.md).  Whether a person is a citizen of Singapore is a status borrowed
-- from outside the Act, stated as a fact.  Limb (c) names criteria in regulations
-- that are not among the sources, so the person states whether they are met;
-- NOTHING means that is not known.
-- src:257 | 6.—(1) In this Act, an eligible individual is an individual who —
-- src:259 | (a) is a citizen of Singapore;
-- src:261 | (b) has attained 65 years of age; and
-- src:263 | (c) satisfies all other eligibility criteria that may be prescribed.
@ref SSSA2015 s 6(1) (src:257-263)
GIVEN `the individual is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      birth IS A `Birth facts`
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the individual satisfies all other eligibility criteria that may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an eligible individual is an individual who — (a) is a citizen of Singapore"
        IF NOT `the individual is a citizen of Singapore` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) has attained 65 years of age"
        IF `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` birth `the date asked about` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) satisfies all other eligibility criteria that may be prescribed"
        IF `the individual satisfies all other eligibility criteria that may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the age limb cannot be worked out without the year of birth
        IF `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` birth `the date asked about` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the criteria that may be prescribed are in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `the individual satisfies all other eligibility criteria that may be prescribed` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 7 Benefits`

-- s 7(1): "An eligible individual is eligible to receive such benefits in such
-- manner and of such amounts as may be prescribed".  The grant is to an
-- eligible individual; a person who is not one falls outside the limit of the
-- grant, and the text does not say that such a person is not eligible to receive
-- anything, so that answer is NOTHING, not FALSE (marginal reading (b)).
-- src:284 | 7.—(1) An eligible individual is eligible to receive such benefits in
-- src:285 | such manner and of such amounts as may be prescribed.
@ref SSSA2015 s 7(1) (src:284-285)
GIVEN eligible IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` MEANS
    CONSIDER eligible
    WHEN JUST isEligible THEN
        IF isEligible
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "An eligible individual" and says nothing of anyone else
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the individual is an eligible individual turns on criteria that may be prescribed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The amount: "of such amounts as may be prescribed".  The amount is a number
-- in regulations that are not among the sources; the caller states it.
-- src:284 | 7.—(1) An eligible individual is eligible to receive such benefits in
-- src:285 | such manner and of such amounts as may be prescribed.
@ref SSSA2015 s 7(1) (src:284-285)
GIVEN eligible IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(1) the amount of benefit an eligible individual is eligible to receive` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` eligible EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `the amount prescribed`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only an eligible individual is given the amounts prescribed
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The manner: "in such manner ... as may be prescribed".
-- src:284 | 7.—(1) An eligible individual is eligible to receive such benefits in
-- src:285 | such manner and of such amounts as may be prescribed.
@ref SSSA2015 s 7(1) (src:284-285)
GIVEN eligible IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the manner prescribed` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 7(1) the manner in which an eligible individual is to receive the benefit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` eligible EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `the manner prescribed`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only an eligible individual is given the manner prescribed
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 7(2): different benefits, methods and amounts "may be prescribed for
-- different classes of eligible individuals".  The classes and amounts are in
-- regulations that are not among the sources; the caller supplies the table.
-- src:287 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), different benefits, different
-- src:288 | methods of disbursing or conferring benefits and different amounts of
-- src:289 | benefits may be prescribed for different classes of eligible
-- src:290 | individuals.
@ref SSSA2015 s 7(2) (src:287-290)
GIVEN class IS A STRING
      table IS A LIST OF `Class amount`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(2) the amount prescribed for the class of eligible individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER table
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the classes and amounts that may be prescribed are in regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF row's `class of eligible individual` EQUALS class
        THEN JUST (row's `amount prescribed`)
        ELSE `s 7(2) the amount prescribed for the class of eligible individual` class rest
